<?xml version="1.0"?>
<model>
  <name>continuum_arm_rbsn</name>
  <version>1.0</version>
  <sdf version='1.9'>model.sdf</sdf>

  <author>
   <name>Aabhash Bhandari</name>
  </author>

  <description>
    3-tendon soft continuum robotic arm, same geometry/mass/tendon layout
    as continuum_arm_pcc and continuum_arm_cosserat (Ø40mm OD / Ø30mm ID
    lattice-TPU tube, 15 rigid segments over 0.40m, 3 tendons at 120deg on
    a 15mm pitch radius), but the third and most physically distinct
    mechanics model of the three: a Non-Linear Rigid-Body Spring Network
    (RBSN). Instead of kinematic PD-position-tracking (PCC) or a quasi-
    static Cosserat BVP solve tracked by PD (Cosserat), RBSN runs genuine
    forward dynamics - every joint carries its own non-linear elastic
    restoring torque tau_spring(theta)=k1*theta+k2*theta^3 plus linear
    viscous damping, and commanded tendon tension is converted directly
    into a generalized actuation TORQUE (via the tendon-routing Jacobian's
    transpose), not a solved position target. The gz/DART physics engine
    integrates the resulting motion; the arm's bend emerges as a real
    dynamic equilibrium between actuation and the non-linear spring, not
    something a position controller teleports into place.

    Actuated by the RbsnArmController model plugin (see
    plugins/rbsn_arm_controller), which subscribes to the same 3-tendon
    length command convention as the other two models (gz.msgs.Vector3d on
    /continuum_arm_rbsn/tendon_cmd, x=l1, y=l2, z=l3).

    Joint state (actual, physics-integrated angles) is published via the
    stock JointStatePublisher system on /continuum_arm_rbsn/joint_states.

    Mount contract: continuum_arm_rbsn/base_cyl's top face (z=0 in this
    module's own frame) is the attachment interface, matching
    continuum_arm_pcc/continuum_arm_cosserat's identical convention.
  </description>
</model>
